  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Monday)\nIssued at 1255 PM CST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nThe forecast remains unchanged as zonal flow aloft is expected to \ndominate the Long Term period. A weak cold front is expected to move \nthrough the area Thursday, dropping highs 3-5 degrees for most from \nthe previous day. Guidance shows the front reaching the Big Bend \nRegion late Thursday night/early Friday morning. This may bring some \nisolated to scattered showers and storms to the Big Bend Friday \nnight into Saturday. Otherwise, westerly flow aloft keeps the rest \nof the area dry through the extended. Increasing cloud cover in \naddition to surface high pressure over the Central Plains reinforces \ncooler air into the region late week/this weekend, yielding highs in \nthe low to mid 60s for most. Long-range guidance shows an upper \nridge building over west Texas and southeast New Mexico by early \nnext week, indicating the potential start to a warming trend. Though \nit should be noted exactly how much warming takes place is uncertain \ndue to large spread among the ensembles.\n\nGreening",
